"ui" is distinctive in Lojban. "pe" and "be" (and "zed" and "theta") are in 
English.  The fact that your language doesn't have the distinctions involved may 
make English -- or Lojban -- a bit harder for you but doesn't make them less 
distinctive in their own languages.  So, {ky} and {kybu} are quite distinct in 
Lojban, as distinct as {cy} and {ebu}.  Since this is obvious, I fear I am 
missing your point here.


